     },
     {
      "text": "**Classifying central structures**\n\nIn my analysis of the image slices, I'm observing that Slice 8 has a small central object while Slice 9 shows a darker linear feature. I wonder if these artifacts could be generated by AI and further obscured by high-frequency noise. I need to classify the central structure: a nodule would change shape over the slices, while a vessel would maintain a consistent diameter. My estimated diameter is about 8 mm based on my observations across the nine slices, which span 10 mm.",
